1460
00:55:19,115 --> 00:55:20,583
Is it bland?

1461
00:55:20,650 --> 00:55:22,018
-No, not at all.
-No?

1462
00:55:22,085 --> 00:55:25,255
I think everything
has been seasoned perfectly.

1463
00:55:25,322 --> 00:55:27,290
-It's great.
-I see.

1464
00:55:28,124 --> 00:55:31,361
It's such a wonder that
he made this soup in such a short time.

1465
00:55:31,428 --> 00:55:32,696
Right?

1466
00:55:32,762 --> 00:55:35,965
The flavor changed drastically
in just two, three minutes.

1467
00:55:36,032 --> 00:55:37,500
He seasoned it at the end.

1468
00:55:37,567 --> 00:55:39,169
You know what? I'm craving this again.

1469
00:55:39,235 --> 00:55:40,904
OH, HUH?

1470
00:55:40,970 --> 00:55:42,739
-The pot rice?
-This is oddly…

1471
00:55:42,806 --> 00:55:45,141
-…addictive. It's odd.
-Yes, it's addictive.

1472
00:55:46,643 --> 00:55:49,813
It's not too strong,
but you want to go back and eat it.

1473
00:55:49,879 --> 00:55:51,147
PLEASED

1474
00:55:51,214 --> 00:55:52,749
How do you explain that mix?

1475
00:55:52,816 --> 00:55:55,085
You had a plan all along, Sung-jun.

1476
00:55:55,151 --> 00:55:58,421
It's so good. I want to keep eating it,
but I have more dishes to try,

1477
00:55:58,488 --> 00:56:00,423
-so I can't eat much.
-You're right.

1478
00:56:00,490 --> 00:56:02,792
Next, Chef Jong-won's dishes.

1479
00:56:02,859 --> 00:56:04,961
BRAISED ABALONE, OCTOPUS SKEWER

1480
00:56:05,028 --> 00:56:06,796
MEAT JEON

1481
00:56:06,863 --> 00:56:08,131
SHRIMP JEON

1482
00:56:08,198 --> 00:56:09,265
CHINESE YAM JEON

1483
00:56:09,332 --> 00:56:10,734
ZUCCHINI JEON

1484
00:56:11,334 --> 00:56:14,371
BUCHIMGAE MENTORED BY MS. KIM MAE-SUN

1485
00:56:14,904 --> 00:56:17,407
WITH NUTTY AND CLEAN BURDOCK TEA

1486
00:56:18,274 --> 00:56:22,479
CHEF SON JONG-WON'S
A BUCHIMGAE TO REMEMBER

1487
00:56:23,046 --> 00:56:24,647
-Shall I?
-Will you open it?

1488
00:56:25,148 --> 00:56:27,317
Gosh. These are so pretty.

1489
00:56:27,384 --> 00:56:30,220
Everything looks so neat.

1490
00:56:30,286 --> 00:56:32,655
-First, try the zucchini <i>jeon.</i>
-Zucchini.

1491
00:56:32,722 --> 00:56:35,825
It's always meaningful
to make <i>jeon</i> with seasonal ingredients.

1492
00:56:35,892 --> 00:56:36,760
SNIFF

1493
00:56:36,826 --> 00:56:39,829
The zucchini <i>jeon</i> he learned
under Ms. Kim Mae-sun.

1494
00:56:39,896 --> 00:56:41,431
Zucchini <i>jeon</i> is delicious.

1495
00:56:41,998 --> 00:56:43,266
It must be good.

1496
00:56:44,634 --> 00:56:45,902
It's savory.

1497
00:56:46,469 --> 00:56:48,571
Is there a difference with the usual <i>jeon?</i>

1498
00:56:48,638 --> 00:56:49,906
-There is.
-There is?

1499
00:56:49,973 --> 00:56:52,308
First of all, we rarely
pre-season the ingredients.

1500
00:56:52,375 --> 00:56:55,478
If we do, it's usually just salt.

1501
00:56:55,545 --> 00:56:57,280
But there's this umami.

1502
00:56:57,847 --> 00:57:01,718
It might be the <i>aekjeot,</i>
but there's this inexplicable flavor

1503
00:57:01,785 --> 00:57:04,020
that adds a fancy depth to the dish.

1504
00:57:04,087 --> 00:57:06,423
The beauty of Korean cuisine

1505
00:57:06,489 --> 00:57:08,358
isn't in fancy techniques,

1506
00:57:08,425 --> 00:57:10,126
but in graceful elegance.

1507
00:57:10,193 --> 00:57:12,162
Something demure and beautiful.

1508
00:57:12,228 --> 00:57:13,496
Korean cuisine has that depth.

1509
00:57:13,563 --> 00:57:14,798
-It does.
-Yes.

1510
00:57:14,864 --> 00:57:16,266
Should I try the meat next?

1511
00:57:16,332 --> 00:57:18,968
-The meat. Meat <i>jeon.</i>
<i>-</i>Meat <i>jeon.</i>

1512
00:57:20,170 --> 00:57:21,438
The best kind of <i>jeon.</i>

1513
00:57:21,704 --> 00:57:22,639
AMAZED

1514
00:57:22,705 --> 00:57:24,007
Here's what I want to know.

1515
00:57:24,073 --> 00:57:26,075
-He toasted the flour, right?
-Right.

1516
00:57:26,142 --> 00:57:29,112
So does it taste nuttier than usual?

1517
00:57:29,179 --> 00:57:32,348
This batter tastes fantastic.

1518
00:57:32,415 --> 00:57:34,317
It wouldn't matter what it is.

1519
00:57:34,384 --> 00:57:38,288
It'd be delicious
once it's coated with this batter.

1520
00:57:38,354 --> 00:57:41,024
Next, please try the abalone.

1521
00:57:41,090 --> 00:57:42,759
YUM

1522
00:57:42,826 --> 00:57:43,760
Mmm.

1523
00:57:44,327 --> 00:57:45,628
I love how sweet it is.

1524
00:57:45,695 --> 00:57:47,464
-Braised abalone.
-<i>Jeonbok-cho.</i>

1525
00:57:47,730 --> 00:57:49,833
ANOTHER BITE OF ABALONE

1526
00:57:50,400 --> 00:57:51,367
This is just what I like.

1527
00:57:51,434 --> 00:57:53,303
It's just what she likes.

1528
00:57:53,369 --> 00:57:54,737
It's kind of sweet.

1529
00:57:54,804 --> 00:57:56,573
-Emergency.
-And it's adequately cooked.

1530
00:57:57,140 --> 00:57:59,042
Next, have a sip of the burdock tea.

1531
00:57:59,108 --> 00:58:01,177
This is when you have the tea.

1532
00:58:01,244 --> 00:58:03,513
-That looks so nice and nutty.
-You added honey too.

1533
00:58:03,580 --> 00:58:06,115
I roasted burdock without oil,

1534
00:58:06,182 --> 00:58:07,817
then boiled it in water.

1535
00:58:07,884 --> 00:58:12,622
Then I added a drop of homemade soy sauce
and a hint of honey.

1536
00:58:12,689 --> 00:58:15,091
-You'll taste the umami.
-Soy sauce and honey.

1537
00:58:15,625 --> 00:58:16,926
What's the tea like?

1538
00:58:16,993 --> 00:58:18,161
It's delicious.

1539
00:58:18,228 --> 00:58:20,163
-There's depth to it.
-Depth.

1540
00:58:20,230 --> 00:58:22,565
I want to try making this at home.

1541
00:58:23,366 --> 00:58:24,901
It's easy to make too.

1542
00:58:24,968 --> 00:58:26,803
-Is this an octopus skewer?
-Octopus skewer.

1543
00:58:26,870 --> 00:58:29,138
He coated it with some sauce.

1544
00:58:30,707 --> 00:58:32,308
It tastes really smoky.

1545
00:58:32,375 --> 00:58:35,111
-He grilled it over the fire.
-Right over the fire.

1546
00:58:35,178 --> 00:58:36,613
It practically burned.

1547
00:58:36,679 --> 00:58:40,016
When I boil small octopus
or octopus at home,

1548
00:58:40,083 --> 00:58:42,952
I never know how long to cook it.

1549
00:58:43,453 --> 00:58:45,955
It's so hard to create this texture.

1550
00:58:46,022 --> 00:58:48,825
If you have good ingredients,
just blanch it very quickly.

1551
00:58:48,892 --> 00:58:50,727
I love this tender texture.

1552
00:58:50,793 --> 00:58:51,995
Does the flavor change?

1553
00:58:52,061 --> 00:58:54,898
Actors can enunciate perfectly
even with food in their mouths.

1554
00:58:54,964 --> 00:58:55,798
-Yes.
-Right?

1555
00:58:56,432 --> 00:58:57,600
Even with the mouth closed.

1556
00:58:57,667 --> 00:58:59,569
It must be because of these scenes.

1557
00:58:59,802 --> 00:59:00,803
AMAZED

1558
00:59:01,371 --> 00:59:02,539
Comes with experience.

1559
00:59:02,605 --> 00:59:05,475
-We often read our lines while eating.
-Right.

1560
00:59:05,542 --> 00:59:08,278
-Lastly, Chinese yam <i>jeon.</i>
-Chinese yam <i>jeon.</i>

1561
00:59:10,914 --> 00:59:12,482
CHEWY

1562
00:59:14,584 --> 00:59:16,819
I can smell something different.

1563
00:59:16,886 --> 00:59:19,155
I topped it
with a bit of <i>saeujeot,</i> salted shrimp.

1564
00:59:19,222 --> 00:59:20,189
<i>Saeujeot?</i>

1565
00:59:21,224 --> 00:59:22,125
He used <i>saeujeot?</i>

1566
00:59:22,191 --> 00:59:23,026
Only for this one?

1567
00:59:23,092 --> 00:59:24,661
Yes, only on Chinese yam.

1568
00:59:24,727 --> 00:59:27,664
But it doesn't taste like <i>saeujeot.</i>

1569
00:59:27,730 --> 00:59:29,632
I'm just wondering what it is,
but it's so good.

1570
00:59:31,200 --> 00:59:33,970
Chinese yam is mostly about its texture.

1571
00:59:34,037 --> 00:59:35,705
-It's crunchy.
-It doesn't taste like much.

1572
00:59:35,772 --> 00:59:39,576
So a pinch of salted shrimp
will bring out a lot of flavor.

1573
00:59:39,642 --> 00:59:42,211
Also, shrimp flavors are brought out

1574
00:59:42,278 --> 00:59:44,847
-when they're cooked in oil.
-It has to be delicious.

1575
00:59:44,914 --> 00:59:46,215
Chinese yams are great when cooked.

1576
00:59:47,016 --> 00:59:48,851
Chinese yam <i>jeon</i> was a new experience.

1577
00:59:48,918 --> 00:59:50,019
It was different.

1578
00:59:50,086 --> 00:59:53,089
How many flavors
did you just let her experience?

1579
00:59:53,590 --> 00:59:55,258
All right, then.

1580
00:59:55,325 --> 00:59:58,728
-How am I going to choose?
-Right?

1581
00:59:58,795 --> 01:00:00,463
-It must be tough.
-Yes.

1582
01:00:00,530 --> 01:00:01,965
But she needs to do it.

1583
01:00:02,031 --> 01:00:04,167
All right. Please make your decision.

1584
01:00:04,233 --> 01:00:06,336
-This is tough.
-Time to decide.

1585
01:00:06,402 --> 01:00:07,470
<i>Press one for Jong-won.</i>

1586
01:00:08,738 --> 01:00:10,273
<i>Press two for Sung-jun.</i>

1587
01:00:11,074 --> 01:00:12,375
Make your decision

1588
01:00:12,442 --> 01:00:14,010
and press the button!

1589
01:00:14,077 --> 01:00:15,378
WIGGLING

1590
01:00:15,445 --> 01:00:18,381
This is too harsh.

1591
01:00:18,448 --> 01:00:20,650
Even a home cook like me

1592
01:00:20,717 --> 01:00:23,586
gets a bit disappointed
when my son and husband

1593
01:00:23,653 --> 01:00:25,321
-don't look excited.
-Yes.

1594
01:00:25,388 --> 01:00:27,991
-So I keep asking them.
-You're right.

1595
01:00:28,057 --> 01:00:30,026
-You need that response.
-Until they tell me.

1596
01:00:30,093 --> 01:00:31,794
That's why I'm feeling

1597
01:00:32,362 --> 01:00:34,864
-really sad right now.
-I see.

1598
01:00:36,966 --> 01:00:38,534
-Okay. I did.
-Make your choice.

1599
01:00:38,601 --> 01:00:40,069
-She pressed one.
-You did?

1600
01:00:40,136 --> 01:00:42,839
Let's find out the result. Show us.

1601
01:00:43,539 --> 01:00:46,075
This round
was between Sung-jun and Jong-won.

1602
01:00:46,142 --> 01:00:49,746
Will Jong-won win the star

1603
01:00:49,812 --> 01:00:51,547
and continue to race forward?

1604
01:00:51,614 --> 01:00:53,750
Or will Sung-jun win

1605
01:00:53,816 --> 01:00:58,221
and seize his buzzworthiness once again?

1606
01:00:58,287 --> 01:01:01,391
Who did Ye-jin choose?

1607
01:01:01,457 --> 01:01:04,861
Someone Who Cooks Well for Her Guests.

1608
01:01:04,927 --> 01:01:06,829
KWON SUNG-JUN WINS

1609
01:01:07,063 --> 01:01:08,464
NO LOSING CHOICE WINS

1610
01:01:08,531 --> 01:01:09,666
Sung-jun wins.

1611
01:01:10,166 --> 01:01:12,769
She picked Kwon Sung-jun.

1612
01:01:12,835 --> 01:01:14,804
-No Losing Chance!
-No Losing Chance!

1613
01:01:14,871 --> 01:01:15,872
Wait, me?

1614
01:01:16,372 --> 01:01:17,540
It was in the name.

1615
01:01:17,607 --> 01:01:19,175
Was there a difference?

1616
01:01:19,242 --> 01:01:22,445
Every single item
on Chef Jong-won's dish was delicious,

1617
01:01:22,512 --> 01:01:23,579
but I decided

1618
01:01:23,646 --> 01:01:27,550
on the fact that he made this soup
in such a short time.

1619
01:01:27,617 --> 01:01:29,385
And it also tasted like
squid soup, my favorite.

1620
01:01:29,452 --> 01:01:31,087
Squid soup.

1621
01:01:31,320 --> 01:01:32,722
GOOD ONE

1622
01:01:32,789 --> 01:01:36,092
He didn't even use a squid,
but it still had that flavor.

1623
01:01:36,159 --> 01:01:38,795
Also, this pot rice

1624
01:01:38,861 --> 01:01:42,298
will seem like a novelty
when I serve it to people,

1625
01:01:42,365 --> 01:01:44,567
-and they'll enjoy it.
-Of course.

1626
01:01:44,634 --> 01:01:46,936
Sung-jun, who never has guests over,

1627
01:01:47,003 --> 01:01:49,806
-Not even once.
-…wins against Jong-won,

1628
01:01:49,872 --> 01:01:53,109
who had been entertaining guests
since age 18.

1629
01:01:53,176 --> 01:01:54,310
It must feel unfair.

1630
01:01:54,377 --> 01:01:56,045
It must feel unfair for you.

1631
01:01:56,112 --> 01:01:58,848
And so, Ye-jin chose

1632
01:01:58,915 --> 01:02:01,084
Chef Sung-jun's dish.

1633
01:02:01,651 --> 01:02:03,619
-Great work.
-That was his ninth win.

1634
01:02:03,686 --> 01:02:05,421
And you'll get the facial masks.

1635
01:02:05,621 --> 01:02:07,223
JEALOUS

1636
01:02:07,290 --> 01:02:10,193
He'll need two sheets per session.

1637
01:02:10,259 --> 01:02:12,261
HIS SUJEBI FACE ISSUE

1638
01:02:12,328 --> 01:02:16,065
-It's his ninth win, only one shy of ten.
-Ninth win?

1639
01:02:16,132 --> 01:02:17,200
-Yes.
-Thank you.

1640
01:02:17,266 --> 01:02:19,302
And the present for Sung-jun.

1641
01:02:19,368 --> 01:02:21,604
-Congratulations.
-Thank you.

1642
01:02:22,905 --> 01:02:25,174
He takes Jong-won down yet again.

1643
01:02:25,241 --> 01:02:29,245
<i>This is the second cook-off</i>
<i>played with Ye-jin's fridge.</i>

1644
01:02:29,312 --> 01:02:31,214
The crazy Chinese sisters,

1645
01:02:31,280 --> 01:02:32,982
Chef Yi Moon-jung and Park Eun-yeong,

1646
01:02:33,049 --> 01:02:34,851
versus the new Western teacher-pupil team,

1647
01:02:34,917 --> 01:02:38,554
Chef Choi Hyun-suk and Yoon Nam-no.

1648
01:02:38,621 --> 01:02:41,724
I'm looking forward to seeing
all kinds of ruckus.

1649
01:02:41,791 --> 01:02:45,461
-We have something Nam-no said alone.
-What is it?

1650
01:02:45,528 --> 01:02:47,797
"Today's my day
on Daddy Hyun-suk's wagon."

1651
01:02:48,364 --> 01:02:50,399
-Daddy Hyun-suk's wagon?
-What do you mean?

1652
01:02:50,466 --> 01:02:52,769
Like how Korean soccer pioneers
were often called dads,

1653
01:02:52,835 --> 01:02:55,571
<i>CCW</i> had another dad, Daddy Hyun-suk.

1654
01:02:55,638 --> 01:02:57,140
During <i>CCW Season 1,</i>

1655
01:02:57,206 --> 01:03:00,476
he was the one who got me
to the semifinals.

1656
01:03:00,543 --> 01:03:02,845
Hyun-suk's looking out into the distance.

1657
01:03:02,912 --> 01:03:05,715
-He kept driving the wagon for us.
-You've hitchhiked.

1658
01:03:05,782 --> 01:03:08,017
-He gave you a ride.
-He was on a roll.

1659
01:03:08,084 --> 01:03:10,019
I did awfully during that mission

1660
01:03:10,086 --> 01:03:11,821
and made many mistakes.

1661
01:03:11,888 --> 01:03:15,591
But next to me, he kept saying,
"It's okay. Just listen to me."

1662
01:03:15,658 --> 01:03:16,659
DADDY HYUN-SUK SAVED HIM

1663
01:03:16,726 --> 01:03:20,663
Nam-no is the type
who does hustle play, right?

1664
01:03:20,730 --> 01:03:22,398
He had to be gentle with the risotto,

1665
01:03:22,465 --> 01:03:25,501
but he went rogue
and destroyed those grains.

1666
01:03:25,568 --> 01:03:27,436
He destroyed them?

1667
01:03:27,503 --> 01:03:29,972
-I've never shared this story elsewhere.
-You're right.

1668
01:03:30,039 --> 01:03:31,474
But during the ride,

1669
01:03:31,541 --> 01:03:33,743
didn't Hyun-suk jump off the wagon first?

1670
01:03:34,610 --> 01:03:36,078
OH…

1671
01:03:36,145 --> 01:03:39,115
-He was driving quite safely.
-It was a smooth ride.

1672
01:03:39,182 --> 01:03:42,318
Then he suddenly ditched the wheel
and jumped off.

1673
01:03:42,385 --> 01:03:43,719
He got off first, right?

1674
01:03:43,786 --> 01:03:45,188
That's the father's role.

1675
01:03:45,588 --> 01:03:46,889
MOVED…

1676
01:03:46,956 --> 01:03:49,225
-I've given…
-"I forgot garlic at home!"

1677
01:03:49,292 --> 01:03:52,428
…my children a ride to their destination,

1678
01:03:52,495 --> 01:03:53,729
so the dad had to leave.

1679
01:03:53,796 --> 01:03:55,131
KNOWS WHEN TO LEAVE

1680
01:03:55,198 --> 01:03:57,934
Thanks to him, I took fourth place.

1681
01:03:58,000 --> 01:04:02,205
So Hyun-suk took eighth place
and helped his son reach fourth place.

1682
01:04:02,271 --> 01:04:04,207
Even for this team round,

1683
01:04:04,273 --> 01:04:07,310
Chef Nam-no is pretty much
in for a free ride.

1684
01:04:07,376 --> 01:04:08,477
No.

1685
01:04:08,544 --> 01:04:10,179
-We're in this together.
-Is that so?

1686
01:04:10,246 --> 01:04:12,782
But do not try to lead the way.

1687
01:04:12,849 --> 01:04:13,916
Just do as you're told.

1688
01:04:13,983 --> 01:04:15,117
ANSWER ME, SON!

1689
01:04:15,184 --> 01:04:17,053
-Yes, sir!
-"Don't be stubborn."

1690
01:04:17,119 --> 01:04:19,455
-Yes, sir!
-"No talking back."

1691
01:04:19,522 --> 01:04:21,457
Not Daddy Hyun-suk, but Grandpa Hyun-suk

1692
01:04:21,524 --> 01:04:23,626
will let you jump on my wagon,

1693
01:04:23,693 --> 01:04:25,795
-so come along for an easy ride.
-Yes!

1694
01:04:25,862 --> 01:04:28,397
BUT WE WON'T LET THAT HAPPEN

1695
01:04:28,464 --> 01:04:31,801
-The sisters lost the last team round.
-They did.

1696
01:04:31,868 --> 01:04:34,036
I'm not sure if reuniting is a good idea.

1697
01:04:34,103 --> 01:04:37,240
We were too focused on performing.

1698
01:04:37,306 --> 01:04:41,177
THEIR PERFORMANCES SURELY WERE INTRIGUING

1699
01:04:41,244 --> 01:04:43,412
I asked, "What's more important?

1700
01:04:43,479 --> 01:04:45,114
Star or buzz?"

1701
01:04:45,181 --> 01:04:46,983
-You did? And?
-Yes.

1702
