1942
01:13:50,793 --> 01:13:51,627
He'll…

1943
01:13:51,693 --> 01:13:54,563
What was that
rolling technique called again?

1944
01:13:54,630 --> 01:13:55,464
<i>Involtini.</i>

1945
01:13:55,531 --> 01:13:57,332
-It's called <i>involtini.</i>
<i>-Involtini.</i>

1946
01:13:57,399 --> 01:14:00,869
He'll steam it or roast it in the oven.

1947
01:14:00,936 --> 01:14:02,037
Grill it or oven-roast it.

1948
01:14:02,104 --> 01:14:04,573
<i>Involtini.</i> Six minutes.

1949
01:14:04,640 --> 01:14:05,607
It looks great.

1950
01:14:05,674 --> 01:14:06,642
INTO THE OVEN

1951
01:14:07,342 --> 01:14:09,578
-Eun-yeong deep-fries the eggplant.
-Yes.

1952
01:14:09,645 --> 01:14:13,449
-It looks good.
-It's Eun-yeong in pigtails.

1953
01:14:13,515 --> 01:14:16,485
-The one who had Ye-jin as her inspo.
-Inspo.

1954
01:14:16,552 --> 01:14:20,923
I think that fried eggplant
will become a nest.

1955
01:14:20,989 --> 01:14:23,559
-It must be the nest.
-She's using a strainer.

1956
01:14:23,625 --> 01:14:26,395
She's spreading it out like a nest.

1957
01:14:26,462 --> 01:14:29,565
Moon-jung puts lots of work into the nest.

1958
01:14:29,631 --> 01:14:32,234
Can she keep those fixed?

1959
01:14:32,301 --> 01:14:34,536
It'll be bad news
if it gets stuck on the strainer.

1960
01:14:34,603 --> 01:14:37,473
-Really.
-If it gets stuck on it.

1961
01:14:37,539 --> 01:14:39,241
It should fall apart right away.

1962
01:14:39,308 --> 01:14:41,977
-Yes.
-It'll stay in that shape.

1963
01:14:42,277 --> 01:14:43,545
MEANWHILE…

1964
01:14:43,612 --> 01:14:45,047
That's burning.

1965
01:14:45,113 --> 01:14:46,648
-What's burning?
-Burning?

1966
01:14:46,715 --> 01:14:48,250
-What's burning?
-Burning?

1967
01:14:48,584 --> 01:14:50,118
SUGAR EMERGENCY

1968
01:14:50,185 --> 01:14:51,353
It's burnt.

1969
01:14:51,420 --> 01:14:52,788
Let it burn.

1970
01:14:52,855 --> 01:14:53,789
It's burnt.

1971
01:14:53,856 --> 01:14:55,591
Sugar. Sugar's burning.

1972
01:14:55,657 --> 01:14:57,426
-Don't stir it.
-Just one side.

1973
01:14:57,493 --> 01:14:59,194
Can you use that?

1974
01:14:59,261 --> 01:15:00,629
No, you can't. Do it over.

1975
01:15:00,696 --> 01:15:02,231
Do it over!

1976
01:15:02,297 --> 01:15:04,600
-You have to redo it.
-Eun-yeong looks lost.

1977
01:15:04,666 --> 01:15:06,802
-Moon-jung looks furious.
-No, we can stir it.

1978
01:15:06,869 --> 01:15:08,070
I'll teach you how to make <i>basi.</i>

1979
01:15:08,303 --> 01:15:09,872
STIRRING…

1980
01:15:09,938 --> 01:15:12,241
If that's burnt,
pull out a pan and start over.

1981
01:15:12,307 --> 01:15:13,942
It'd better to redo it.

1982
01:15:14,009 --> 01:15:16,879
-She's doing it over.
-Eun-yeong's mistake.

1983
01:15:16,945 --> 01:15:18,714
The moment one side burns,
it keeps burning

1984
01:15:18,780 --> 01:15:21,283
-and makes it taste charred.
-It was a big mistake.

1985
01:15:21,350 --> 01:15:24,286
-That was big.
-Unless it's evenly melted.

1986
01:15:24,353 --> 01:15:25,554
You can't use that.

1987
01:15:25,621 --> 01:15:28,123
Ye-jin even said she loved <i>basi.</i>

1988
01:15:28,724 --> 01:15:29,691
SHE WORKS ON THE NEST FOR NOW

1989
01:15:29,758 --> 01:15:31,860
Moon-jung's nest.

1990
01:15:31,927 --> 01:15:34,129
-You can add some oil.
-Careful.

1991
01:15:34,196 --> 01:15:36,331
Just add some oil.

1992
01:15:37,399 --> 01:15:39,234
What's Hyun-suk up to?

1993
01:15:39,301 --> 01:15:43,705
It looks like he'll make
lasagna with grilled eggplant.

1994
01:15:45,007 --> 01:15:47,309
CHECKING THE EGGPLANT PURÉE

1995
01:15:47,709 --> 01:15:50,479
ASKING THE DRIVER TO CHECK

1996
01:15:51,046 --> 01:15:52,281
It needs to be sweeter.

1997
01:15:52,347 --> 01:15:53,448
More?

1998
01:15:53,515 --> 01:15:54,383
Keep boiling it down.

1999
01:15:54,716 --> 01:15:56,952
BACK TO BOILING IT DOWN!

2000
01:15:57,553 --> 01:15:59,221
ADD MORE FIG JAM

2001
01:15:59,288 --> 01:16:00,956
-You have to keep boiling it down.
-Yes, sir.

2002
01:16:01,123 --> 01:16:02,291
GLANCES

2003
01:16:02,591 --> 01:16:08,130
9. TOP EGGPLANT LASAGNA WITH BÉCHAMEL,
MEAT SAUCE, AND PARMESAN

2004
01:16:08,297 --> 01:16:11,066
LASAGNA GOES INTO THE OVEN TOO!

2005
01:16:11,133 --> 01:16:13,168
-Five minutes.
-Five minutes left.

2006
01:16:13,235 --> 01:16:15,170
-Five minutes.
-Please make your way over there.

2007
01:16:15,237 --> 01:16:17,072
-Keep boiling it.
-There's not enough time.

2008
01:16:17,139 --> 01:16:19,474
-Fry these too.
-It's so hectic with four people.

2009
01:16:19,541 --> 01:16:22,411
I'm hoping to see the nest.
The eggplant nest.

2010
01:16:22,477 --> 01:16:24,546
-Is the nest ready?
-The nest.

2011
01:16:24,613 --> 01:16:26,114
-The nest.
-The nest.

2012
01:16:26,181 --> 01:16:29,551
-She's trying to pull it off.
-It's not coming off?

2013
01:16:29,618 --> 01:16:32,654
-Moon-jung's nest!
-It's about to break.

2014
01:16:33,221 --> 01:16:34,389
-She can't pull it off.
-The nest.

2015
01:16:34,456 --> 01:16:35,290
The nest.

2016
01:16:35,724 --> 01:16:37,359
EVERYONE'S TALKING ABOUT THE NEST

2017
01:16:37,426 --> 01:16:39,227
-The nest.
-It won't come off!

2018
01:16:39,294 --> 01:16:40,562
The nest won't come off.

2019
01:16:40,629 --> 01:16:41,530
Moon-jung's nest!

2020
01:16:41,597 --> 01:16:43,065
IT WORKED!

2021
01:16:43,332 --> 01:16:44,566
Slam the bottom.

2022
01:16:44,633 --> 01:16:47,002
-It came off.
-It did? Okay.

2023
01:16:47,069 --> 01:16:49,237
She almost served it on the strainer.

2024
01:16:50,105 --> 01:16:51,740
Make sure you drop the strainer.

2025
01:16:51,807 --> 01:16:53,008
TREATING A VIP POORLY

2026
01:16:53,075 --> 01:16:54,710
You don't have enough time to make <i>basi.</i>

2027
01:16:54,776 --> 01:16:56,578
<i>Basi.</i> The sugar won't melt.

2028
01:16:56,645 --> 01:16:58,246
Hurry and make the <i>basi.</i>

2029
01:16:58,547 --> 01:17:00,248
MY BASI…

2030
01:17:00,315 --> 01:17:01,550
-Three and a half minutes.
-What now?

2031
01:17:01,617 --> 01:17:03,285
-It's okay. Take your time.
-Slowly.

2032
01:17:03,352 --> 01:17:04,720
-Okay.
-Move that and set the plates.

2033
01:17:06,054 --> 01:17:07,322
ASSISTING LIKE A GOOD BOY

2034
01:17:07,389 --> 01:17:08,557
Three minutes.

2035
01:17:08,624 --> 01:17:10,859
-Nam-no begins to plate the dish.
-Nam-no.

2036
01:17:10,926 --> 01:17:12,794
-Are you doing as you're told?
-Yes.

2037
01:17:12,861 --> 01:17:14,229
GETTING BURRATA READY

2038
01:17:14,296 --> 01:17:16,064
The sugar is still not ready.

2039
01:17:16,665 --> 01:17:18,600
They have less than three minutes.

2040
01:17:18,667 --> 01:17:20,969
-Coat it in sugar.
-It's burning.

2041
01:17:21,036 --> 01:17:23,338
-Is this side burnt?
-Just start stirring.

2042
01:17:23,405 --> 01:17:24,706
That's good. Take it off!

2043
01:17:24,773 --> 01:17:26,642
-Take it off the heat.
-That's fine.

2044
01:17:26,708 --> 01:17:27,709
Careful.

2045
01:17:27,776 --> 01:17:30,646
-Eun-yeong needs to step it up.
-You have to make the <i>basi.</i>

2046
01:17:30,712 --> 01:17:33,315
-Careful.
-Things are not going smooth on this side.

2047
01:17:33,382 --> 01:17:34,583
-Get it out.
-What's this?

2048
01:17:34,650 --> 01:17:35,884
I'll finish this off.

2049
01:17:35,951 --> 01:17:37,085
Go ahead.

2050
01:17:37,586 --> 01:17:39,855
-The eggplants were fried nicely.
-Eggplant fritters.

2051
01:17:39,921 --> 01:17:41,723
-That's too much sauce.
-That's <i>basi.</i>

2052
01:17:41,790 --> 01:17:42,924
Two and a half minutes.

2053
01:17:43,158 --> 01:17:45,027
WHAT ABOUT TEAM WESTERN CUISINE?

2054
01:17:45,160 --> 01:17:46,662
CHOPPING BURRATA

2055
01:17:47,229 --> 01:17:48,163
One second.

2056
01:17:48,230 --> 01:17:49,731
-Is this the lasagna plate?
-Yes.

2057
01:17:49,798 --> 01:17:50,699
PLATES IT

2058
01:17:50,766 --> 01:17:52,434
Try the purée. Is it okay?

2059
01:17:52,501 --> 01:17:53,335
The purée.

2060
01:17:53,402 --> 01:17:56,438
-Jung-hwan, try what they're trying.
-The purée.

2061
01:17:56,505 --> 01:17:58,140
They're both trying it.

2062
01:17:58,206 --> 01:18:00,042
-Hyun-suk tried it.
-Which one?

2063
01:18:00,108 --> 01:18:02,544
-"Try this one."
-Which one? The purée?

2064
01:18:03,045 --> 01:18:04,780
TASTING THE PURÉE!

2065
01:18:04,846 --> 01:18:06,782
What's the purée like?

2066
01:18:06,848 --> 01:18:09,685
Does it taste good enough
to help Nam-no win?

2067
01:18:09,751 --> 01:18:11,553
WILL IT HELP NAM-NO FREE-RIDE?

2068
01:18:12,120 --> 01:18:13,855
It's not a smooth journey.

2069
01:18:13,922 --> 01:18:15,457
It tastes a bit burnt.

2070
01:18:15,524 --> 01:18:16,792
-I did burn it.
-You burnt it?

2071
01:18:16,858 --> 01:18:18,427
Then it's right.

2072
01:18:18,493 --> 01:18:20,796
-But it tastes a bit burnt.
-Was it intentional?

2073
01:18:20,862 --> 01:18:22,397
The technique is to add

2074
01:18:22,464 --> 01:18:24,499
the smoky note like charred sweet potato.

2075
01:18:24,566 --> 01:18:27,836
It's like the charred taste
on the outer layer of a sweet potato.

2076
01:18:27,903 --> 01:18:30,105
But the guest has to like it.

2077
01:18:30,172 --> 01:18:32,007
-So he created the smoky flavor.
-Yes.

2078
01:18:32,074 --> 01:18:34,209
-Smoked eggplant sauce tastes burnt.
-It does.

2079
01:18:34,276 --> 01:18:37,245
-So it should be fine.
-It's supposed to be like that.

2080
01:18:37,312 --> 01:18:39,781
He puts lots of work into the purée.

2081
01:18:39,848 --> 01:18:42,250
-Can you chop arugula? Let's grind it.
-Okay.

2082
01:18:42,317 --> 01:18:44,853
We don't have more arugula.

2083
01:18:44,920 --> 01:18:46,221
Never mind, then.

2084
01:18:46,521 --> 01:18:48,223
WHAT WILL NAM-NO DO?

2085
01:18:48,290 --> 01:18:49,958
Should I use a green onion?

2086
01:18:50,025 --> 01:18:51,860
Green onion. The green portion.

2087
01:18:51,927 --> 01:18:54,196
Chop them into tiny circular shapes.

2088
01:18:54,362 --> 01:18:56,665
SMART IMPROVISATION

2089
01:18:57,399 --> 01:18:58,734
-I'll cool it with ice.
-Is it ready?

2090
01:18:59,034 --> 01:19:01,670
GET ICE FROM THE FREEZER

2091
01:19:01,737 --> 01:19:04,439
That's too much oil.

2092
01:19:05,006 --> 01:19:06,508
MIX THE TWO BATCHES!

2093
01:19:06,575 --> 01:19:08,143
Cool it over this for a moment.

2094
01:19:09,211 --> 01:19:11,012
COOLING OVER ICE

2095
01:19:11,079 --> 01:19:12,547
Get the <i>basi</i> in there.

2096
01:19:12,614 --> 01:19:13,448
But not everything.

2097
01:19:14,015 --> 01:19:16,618
Do that first and finish up the gelato.

2098
01:19:16,685 --> 01:19:19,020
-A minute and a half.
-<i>Basi.</i>

2099
01:19:19,087 --> 01:19:20,555
You have a minute and a half.

2100
01:19:20,622 --> 01:19:22,390
What are you putting on the nest?

2101
01:19:22,457 --> 01:19:25,727
-Take it easy. It's okay.
-Eggplant <i>basi.</i>

2102
01:19:25,794 --> 01:19:28,163
Wait, that'll harden the sugar right away.

2103
01:19:28,230 --> 01:19:30,265
She'll harden it and cover it up.

2104
01:19:30,332 --> 01:19:31,900
She'll cover it?

2105
01:19:31,967 --> 01:19:34,236
LIKE THIS!

2106
01:19:34,302 --> 01:19:36,304
Wait, can she do that?

2107
01:19:36,371 --> 01:19:38,073
-It'll be like candy.
-It won't fall out.

2108
01:19:38,140 --> 01:19:40,575
-Is it falling out?
-It is.

2109
01:19:40,642 --> 01:19:41,676
That's just dripping.

2110
01:19:43,712 --> 01:19:45,714
-One minute.
-It's coming undone now.

2111
01:19:45,781 --> 01:19:47,716
You can warm it up with a torch.

2112
01:19:47,783 --> 01:19:49,918
-So that's how.
-You need way more sauce.

2113
01:19:49,985 --> 01:19:51,086
Oh, darn.

2114
01:19:51,153 --> 01:19:52,420
Oh, darn.

2115
01:19:52,487 --> 01:19:56,291
-She said, "Oh, darn."
-She became agitated!

2116
01:19:56,358 --> 01:19:58,360
She's agitated!

2117
01:19:58,426 --> 01:20:00,929
-It cooled too much.
-Oh, darn. The <i>basi.</i>

2118
01:20:01,596 --> 01:20:03,465
COULDN'T HIDE HER FRUSTRATION

2119
01:20:03,532 --> 01:20:04,666
-<i>Basi.</i>
-Give me a little.

2120
01:20:06,268 --> 01:20:07,202
GREEN ONION NAM-NO CHOPPED

2121
01:20:07,269 --> 01:20:08,503
OLIVE OIL

2122
01:20:08,570 --> 01:20:09,938
One minute.

2123
01:20:10,005 --> 01:20:12,440
AND EGGPLANT LASAGNA!

2124
01:20:13,742 --> 01:20:15,377
HYUN-SUK & NAM-NO FINISH FIRST

2125
01:20:15,443 --> 01:20:18,079
-Hyun-suk's team is done.
-Yay!

2126
01:20:18,146 --> 01:20:19,781
-Gelato.
-Thirty-five seconds.

2127
01:20:19,848 --> 01:20:21,583
-Moon-jung.
-Hurry up.

2128
01:20:22,150 --> 01:20:22,984
All right.

2129
01:20:23,051 --> 01:20:24,452
PANICKING

2130
01:20:24,519 --> 01:20:26,154
It's too hard already.

2131
01:20:26,221 --> 01:20:28,456
-That itself is <i>basi.</i>
-<i>Basi.</i>

2132
01:20:28,523 --> 01:20:30,425
-The melted sugar won't fall down.
-This is tough.

2133
01:20:30,492 --> 01:20:31,927
-Right now.
-Right away.

2134
01:20:31,993 --> 01:20:33,094
Just use honey!

2135
01:20:33,161 --> 01:20:36,031
-Put them in and mix.
-Hold it.

2136
01:20:36,097 --> 01:20:37,432
What about the <i>basi?</i> Ten.

2137
01:20:37,499 --> 01:20:38,633
-Just sprinkle some sugar!
-Nine.

2138
01:20:38,700 --> 01:20:39,634
-It's okay.
-Eight.

2139
01:20:40,135 --> 01:20:42,437
WHAT WILL HAPPEN TO THIS BASI?

2140
01:20:42,504 --> 01:20:43,371
It's okay.

2141
01:20:43,438 --> 01:20:45,073
Four. Three.

2142
01:20:45,140 --> 01:20:46,308
-Bring them out.
-Two.

2143
01:20:46,374 --> 01:20:47,409
-One.
-One.

2144
01:20:47,475 --> 01:20:48,610
-Time's up.
-Time's up.

2145
01:20:49,177 --> 01:20:50,545
That's it. Ring the bell.

2146
01:20:50,612 --> 01:20:51,980
-She did.
-That was it.

2147
01:20:52,047 --> 01:20:53,548
Moon-jung and Eun-yeong are done.

2148
01:20:53,615 --> 01:20:57,385
-The sugar's there, just not a lot.
-Is it?

2149
01:20:57,919 --> 01:20:59,588
THE DISHES CAME OUT ALL RIGHT…

2150
01:20:59,654 --> 01:21:01,256
I only remember her swearing.

2151
01:21:01,590 --> 01:21:03,658
REMEMBERING HER "OH, DARN"

2152
01:21:03,725 --> 01:21:05,827
-Yes.
-Did I do that?

2153
01:21:05,894 --> 01:21:08,096
We saw Moon-jung's rough side.

2154
01:21:08,163 --> 01:21:12,033
All eggplant dishes were made for Ye-jin.

2155
01:21:12,100 --> 01:21:15,637
She looks quite excited.
These dishes were finished first.

2156
01:21:16,004 --> 01:21:19,808
EGGPLANT LASAGNA WITH BURRATA

2157
01:21:20,775 --> 01:21:23,511
STRIP LOIN STEAK WRAPPED WITH EGGPLANT

2158
01:21:24,713 --> 01:21:27,282
AND SMOKY EGGPLANT PURÉE

2159
01:21:28,450 --> 01:21:32,354
CHOI HYUN-SUK & YOON NAM-NO'S
I TO YOU AM LIKE EGGPLANTS AT SUNSET

2160
01:21:33,755 --> 01:21:35,824
Wow. What is this?

2161
01:21:35,891 --> 01:21:37,859
Cheese? Burrata.

2162
01:21:37,926 --> 01:21:40,962
Try the eggplant,
sauce, and burrata together.

2163
01:21:41,029 --> 01:21:42,864
Eggplant lasagna.

2164
01:21:42,931 --> 01:21:46,067
So you can make lasagna with eggplants?

2165
01:21:46,134 --> 01:21:47,402
It's pretty common.

2166
01:21:47,469 --> 01:21:48,370
Mmm.

2167
01:21:49,371 --> 01:21:50,272
Mmm.

2168
01:21:51,373 --> 01:21:52,540
-I see.
-Mmm.

2169
01:21:52,607 --> 01:21:54,609
She looks very happy.

2170
01:21:54,676 --> 01:21:57,512
When you mix cold burrata with warm food,

2171
01:21:57,579 --> 01:21:59,314
it brings out the depth in its flavor.

2172
01:22:00,048 --> 01:22:02,617
It tastes so classy.

2173
01:22:02,684 --> 01:22:04,920
And because Ye-jin is eating it now,

2174
01:22:04,986 --> 01:22:07,088
it feels like a first-grade restaurant.

2175
01:22:07,155 --> 01:22:08,990
-"First-grade restaurant"?
-Yes.

2176
01:22:09,057 --> 01:22:10,625
-First-grade restaurant?
-Hey.

2177
01:22:10,692 --> 01:22:11,960
First-grade is the best.

2178
01:22:12,027 --> 01:22:13,295
-It is.
-Of course.

2179
01:22:13,361 --> 01:22:14,930
That's what we said way back when.

2180
01:22:14,996 --> 01:22:16,798
Jeez. You're so ancient.

2181
01:22:17,065 --> 01:22:18,833
MR. ANCIENT IS JUST HAPPY

2182
01:22:20,568 --> 01:22:22,871
She takes a bigger bite this time.

2183
01:22:22,938 --> 01:22:25,640
-That means it's delicious.
-And she likes eggplants.

2184
01:22:25,707 --> 01:22:27,309
-Mmm.
-Yes.

2185
01:22:27,509 --> 01:22:29,177
GULP

2186
01:22:29,244 --> 01:22:32,647
When the sauce is mixed with burrata,
the flavor changes.

2187
01:22:32,714 --> 01:22:34,916
This sauce is delicious too.

2188
01:22:35,150 --> 01:22:36,251
TRYING IT WITH JUST THE SAUCE

2189
01:22:36,318 --> 01:22:38,820
Is it sweet? What's it like?

2190
01:22:38,887 --> 01:22:42,057
What's this sweet flavor? Blueberries?

2191
01:22:42,123 --> 01:22:46,561
<i>-You had fig jam, so I used that.</i>
<i>-Fig jam.</i>

2192
01:22:46,628 --> 01:22:47,796
Mmm.

2193
01:22:47,862 --> 01:22:49,597
That makes this really good.

2194
01:22:49,664 --> 01:22:52,300
Fig jam mixes well with everything.

2195
01:22:52,367 --> 01:22:56,504
Red wine improves meat sauce greatly,

2196
01:22:56,571 --> 01:22:57,639
but you didn't have that,

2197
01:22:57,706 --> 01:23:01,843
<i>so I added blueberries</i>
<i>to give the sauce a bitter note.</i>

2198
01:23:01,910 --> 01:23:04,980
He made use of the tannin from the skins.

2199
01:23:06,114 --> 01:23:09,751
-It's so good.
-That was healthy eggplant lasagna.

2200
01:23:09,818 --> 01:23:12,620
-Next up, the steak.
-As for the steak,

2201
01:23:12,687 --> 01:23:14,155
try it with the purée.

2202
01:23:14,222 --> 01:23:16,558
-Is there steak inside?
-There's steak inside,

2203
01:23:16,624 --> 01:23:18,126
seasoned with parmesan.

2204
01:23:18,193 --> 01:23:19,928
You've wrapped the steak with eggplant.

2205
01:23:19,995 --> 01:23:22,998
And eat it
with the eggplant purée on the side.

2206
01:23:23,064 --> 01:23:24,399
You said it smelled burnt.

2207
01:23:24,466 --> 01:23:27,902
Yes, it smelled like
burnt sweet potato skin.

2208
01:23:27,969 --> 01:23:30,071
She smells it first.

2209
01:23:30,138 --> 01:23:32,440
It doesn't really smell burnt.

2210
01:23:32,507 --> 01:23:33,441
It's smoked.

2211
01:23:33,508 --> 01:23:35,877
-Do you feel uneasy?
-Is this too big?

2212
01:23:35,944 --> 01:23:37,412
-He sounded urgent.
-Yes.

2213
01:23:37,479 --> 01:23:39,748
-Nam-no feels uneasy?
-Yes. Nice job pointing it out.

2214
01:23:40,382 --> 01:23:42,183
LOTS OF EGGPLANT PURÉE

2215
01:23:43,418 --> 01:23:44,819
Is this too big?

2216
01:23:44,886 --> 01:23:46,621
STRAIGHT INTO HER MOUTH

2217
01:23:46,688 --> 01:23:48,723
What's the steak like?

2218
01:23:49,591 --> 01:23:50,692
Mmm.

2219
01:23:50,759 --> 01:23:53,862
Steak wrapped in eggplant
probably tastes different

2220
01:23:53,928 --> 01:23:56,197
from regular steak.

2221
01:23:56,264 --> 01:23:58,533
She took a huge bite.

2222
01:23:58,600 --> 01:24:00,268
It's really good.

2223
01:24:00,468 --> 01:24:02,937
RELIEVED

2224
01:24:03,004 --> 01:24:05,407
I can smell the smokiness,

2225
01:24:05,473 --> 01:24:08,043
and the steak
is cooked perfectly to my liking.

2226
01:24:08,843 --> 01:24:10,445
How did you know?

2227
01:24:10,512 --> 01:24:14,049
It's a little more well done
than a medium.

2228
01:24:14,115 --> 01:24:15,717
It's perfect to my preference.

2229
01:24:15,784 --> 01:24:18,286
-Do you like it past medium?
-Yes.

2230
01:24:18,353 --> 01:24:21,156
-Nothing too tough.
-To cook here at <i>Chef & My Fridge,</i>

2231
01:24:21,222 --> 01:24:23,992
we must study our guests' preferences.

2232
01:24:24,059 --> 01:24:26,428
She didn't tell you, so how did you know?

2233
01:24:26,494 --> 01:24:29,097
If you look around, you'll find a lead.

2234
01:24:29,397 --> 01:24:30,532
MUST'VE BEEN A LUCKY GUESS

2235
01:24:30,598 --> 01:24:31,866
Wasn't it a wild guess?

2236
01:24:31,933 --> 01:24:34,069
Nothing that I do or say

2237
01:24:34,135 --> 01:24:35,603
is a wild guess.

2238
01:24:36,071 --> 01:24:37,405
SURE, WHATEVER…

2239
01:24:37,472 --> 01:24:39,908
I think he's said it once before.

2240
01:24:39,974 --> 01:24:42,777
-But he guessed it perfectly.
-What's this sauce?

2241
01:24:42,844 --> 01:24:44,179
The eggplants we charred.

2242
01:24:44,245 --> 01:24:47,482
<i>We smoked them</i>
<i>to char them like roasted sweet potatoes.</i>

2243
01:24:47,549 --> 01:24:49,617
<i>Then we made them into purée</i>
<i>by mixing them with milk and butter.</i>

2244
01:24:49,684 --> 01:24:53,054
<i>It also won't taste like sweet potato</i>
<i>without sweetness,</i>

2245
01:24:53,121 --> 01:24:55,056
<i>so we added more fig jam there.</i>

2246
01:24:55,123 --> 01:24:57,525
-You added fig jam here too?
-Yes.

2247
01:24:57,592 --> 01:24:58,793
Mmm.

2248
01:24:58,860 --> 01:24:59,794
How's the purée?

2249
01:24:59,861 --> 01:25:01,830
-It's so good.
-Totally?

2250
01:25:01,896 --> 01:25:04,599
And these dishes complement each other,
although they're different.

2251
01:25:04,666 --> 01:25:06,468
<i>This was good by itself,</i>

2252
01:25:06,534 --> 01:25:09,771
<i>and this one was different</i>
<i>with meat inside.</i>

2253
01:25:09,838 --> 01:25:11,306
It was so good.

2254
01:25:11,372 --> 01:25:13,575
Those were the two dishes.

2255
01:25:13,641 --> 01:25:16,544
Next up, Crash Nesting on You.

2256
01:25:16,945 --> 01:25:20,315
EGGPLANT BASI RESTING IN THE NEST

2257
01:25:21,382 --> 01:25:24,519
SERVED WITH EGGPLANT GELATO DESSERT

2258
01:25:25,587 --> 01:25:29,190
LEE MOON-JUNG & PARK EUN-YEONG'S
CRASH NESTING ON YOU

2259
01:25:29,257 --> 01:25:31,860
Eggplants laid eggs in that nest.

2260
01:25:31,926 --> 01:25:33,895
Eggplant eggs in the nest.

2261
01:25:33,962 --> 01:25:38,199
I don't think the <i>basi</i>
turned out like how we expected it to.

2262
01:25:38,266 --> 01:25:40,702
-That in itself is <i>basi.</i>
<i>-</i>It is <i>basi.</i>

2263
01:25:40,768 --> 01:25:42,370
The cooking method is called <i>basi.</i>

2264
01:25:42,437 --> 01:25:45,607
Anything coated with sugar is <i>basi.</i>

2265
01:25:45,673 --> 01:25:46,941
It's like <i>mattang.</i>

2266
01:25:47,008 --> 01:25:48,476
-What's that?
-That's <i>basi.</i>

2267
01:25:48,543 --> 01:25:53,047
You can make it like this
or like what Chef Ji-sun did.

2268
01:25:53,114 --> 01:25:56,384
We're all inclined to think
only Chef Ji-sun's thing is <i>basi.</i>

2269
01:25:56,451 --> 01:25:57,852
CLOSING HER EYES TO SAVOR IT

2270
01:25:58,253 --> 01:25:59,921
TAKING ANOTHER BITE IMMEDIATELY

2271
01:25:59,988 --> 01:26:01,589
It's so good.

2272
01:26:02,090 --> 01:26:03,191
SMILING BACK

2273
01:26:03,258 --> 01:26:05,260
-She said she had a sweet tooth.
-Yes.

2274
01:26:05,326 --> 01:26:08,763
-I like both fried food and sweets.
-This is bad for them.

2275
01:26:08,830 --> 01:26:10,899
-Emergency.
-Sweet and fried.

2276
01:26:10,965 --> 01:26:13,601
I think I can finish this whole thing.

2277
01:26:13,835 --> 01:26:15,003
WOW

2278
01:26:15,203 --> 01:26:16,404
PERFECT TO HER TASTE

2279
01:26:16,471 --> 01:26:17,939
Can she eat the nest too?

2280
01:26:18,006 --> 01:26:19,674
Dip it in the gelato.

2281
01:26:19,741 --> 01:26:21,376
-The gelato?
-This?

2282
01:26:21,442 --> 01:26:25,013
I wanted to put some in the cream,
but I ran out of time.

2283
01:26:25,513 --> 01:26:29,050
I wanted to add a crispy texture,
so I put that in the gelato.

2284
01:26:29,117 --> 01:26:31,586
-Is it an actual gelato?
-Going for her sweet tooth.

2285
01:26:31,786 --> 01:26:33,454
ANOTHER BITE IN SILENCE

2286
01:26:33,521 --> 01:26:34,589
It's not gelato, is it?

2287
01:26:35,223 --> 01:26:36,057
What is it?

2288
01:26:36,124 --> 01:26:37,692
-Hmm…
-Yes?

2289
01:26:37,759 --> 01:26:39,327
Cold porridge?

2290
01:26:39,394 --> 01:26:41,763
No, it's not that. It's like ice cream.

2291
01:26:41,829 --> 01:26:43,264
It's probably not cold enough.

2292
01:26:43,331 --> 01:26:47,769
-It should've sat in there longer.
-It's probably lukewarm.

2293
01:26:47,835 --> 01:26:50,572
-Did you turn it off again?
-As you eat the gelato,

2294
01:26:50,638 --> 01:26:52,073
it will melt over time.

2295
01:26:52,140 --> 01:26:54,108
Then think of it as a dip.

2296
01:26:54,175 --> 01:26:55,076
It's a dip.

2297
01:26:55,143 --> 01:26:58,012
-That's not gelato.
-Chef Moon-jung is

2298
01:26:58,079 --> 01:27:00,615
saying the most random things now.

2299
01:27:01,783 --> 01:27:04,052
-It's so good.
-Is it?

2300
01:27:04,118 --> 01:27:06,287
-It's really good.
-She actually looks happy.

2301
01:27:06,354 --> 01:27:08,756
Look at her.

2302
01:27:08,823 --> 01:27:10,491
She must feel comfortable around us now.

2303
01:27:10,558 --> 01:27:11,893
"This is really good."

2304
01:27:12,093 --> 01:27:13,428
SO FRIENDLY♥

2305
01:27:13,494 --> 01:27:15,163
It's like we're at a casual gathering.

2306
01:27:15,230 --> 01:27:16,831
She goes, "It's so good."

2307
01:27:16,898 --> 01:27:18,866
-"Have some."
-"You have a bite."

2308
01:27:18,933 --> 01:27:20,468
-"It's good."
-Like she's with friends.

2309
01:27:21,369 --> 01:27:23,905
I have a question.

2310
01:27:23,972 --> 01:27:26,241
Is it different from regular <i>basi</i>
and candied sweet potato?

2311
01:27:26,307 --> 01:27:30,878
These are eggplants,
so they're far softer than sweet potatoes.

2312
01:27:30,945 --> 01:27:34,515
It's soft on the inside,
yet crunchy on the outside.

2313
01:27:34,582 --> 01:27:35,984
And it's seasoned well.

2314
01:27:36,851 --> 01:27:39,554
It's not too sweet,
and it was fried perfectly.

2315
01:27:39,621 --> 01:27:42,056
I love things that are fried and sweet.

2316
01:27:42,357 --> 01:27:43,825
FEELING PROUD

2317
01:27:43,891 --> 01:27:46,728
Nam-no, you may not end up with a victory.

2318
01:27:46,794 --> 01:27:49,297
-Emergency.
-They're both good.

2319
01:27:49,364 --> 01:27:52,300
-It's too hard for me to choose.
-They're completely different.

2320
01:27:52,367 --> 01:27:54,869
<i>This is simply something I love,</i>

2321
01:27:54,936 --> 01:27:59,507
and these were really delicious
Western eggplant dishes.

2322
01:27:59,574 --> 01:28:01,943
This is way too harsh on me.

2323
01:28:02,010 --> 01:28:05,847
It's hard to tell how this round will end.

2324
01:28:05,913 --> 01:28:07,015
May I add something?

2325
01:28:07,081 --> 01:28:08,483
-Yes?
-What is it?

2326
01:28:08,549 --> 01:28:10,385
Western nobodies…

2327
01:28:10,451 --> 01:28:12,787
I mean, lousy Western cooks.

2328
01:28:12,854 --> 01:28:15,623
Again, lousy Western cooks rubbed butter

2329
01:28:16,758 --> 01:28:17,859
and Chinese nobodies

2330
01:28:18,660 --> 01:28:20,928
deep-fried eggplants as they always do.

2331
01:28:20,995 --> 01:28:22,363
So which one is new?

2332
01:28:23,264 --> 01:28:24,299
It's the same.

2333
01:28:26,000 --> 01:28:27,935
-They're the same.
-What?

2334
01:28:28,002 --> 01:28:30,004
But I'm truly amazed by the chefs

2335
01:28:30,071 --> 01:28:32,240
for doing this in such a short time.

2336
01:28:33,041 --> 01:28:35,410
They really are amazing.

2337
01:28:35,476 --> 01:28:38,713
When I watched it on TV,
I thought it would be somewhat staged.

2338
01:28:38,780 --> 01:28:41,649
It's impossible for laypeople like us
to cook in 15 minutes, right?

2339
01:28:41,716 --> 01:28:43,384
We'd spend it all on prepping.

2340
01:28:43,451 --> 01:28:47,622
-So I was just blown away.
-That's what they do.

2341
01:28:47,855 --> 01:28:49,257
PUSHING

2342
01:28:49,324 --> 01:28:52,460
When I watched the show,
it was fun to hear the chefs' opinions.

2343
01:28:52,760 --> 01:28:54,362
SHE WANTS TO KNOW WHAT THE CHEFS THINK

2344
01:28:54,429 --> 01:28:55,963
-I'm here as a viewer.
-Pass them around.

2345
01:28:56,030 --> 01:28:59,767
First, Chef Hyun-suk and Nam-no's dish.

2346
01:28:59,834 --> 01:29:02,804
Please try the eggplant steak
and eggplant lasagna.

2347
01:29:02,870 --> 01:29:05,139
-This smoky flavor is really strong.
-Is it?

2348
01:29:05,206 --> 01:29:07,008
-Mmm.
-Let me try it.

2349
01:29:07,075 --> 01:29:08,142
GLANCING

2350
01:29:08,209 --> 01:29:09,110
-What did you try?
-The meat.

2351
01:29:09,177 --> 01:29:10,011
Isn't it delicious?

2352
01:29:10,078 --> 01:29:11,346
-It's cooked so well.
-It's good.

2353
01:29:11,579 --> 01:29:12,914
FEELING PROUD

2354
01:29:12,980 --> 01:29:16,050
The purée tastes different with meat.
It wasn't burnt.

2355
01:29:16,117 --> 01:29:17,418
It doesn't smell burnt.

2356
01:29:17,485 --> 01:29:19,253
It adds a nice charm.

2357
01:29:19,320 --> 01:29:20,855
Did you eat some, Sam?

2358
01:29:20,922 --> 01:29:22,190
-I did.
-What do you think?

2359
01:29:22,256 --> 01:29:23,524
It's good.

2360
01:29:23,725 --> 01:29:25,460
IT MUST BE VERY GOOD

2361
01:29:25,526 --> 01:29:27,362
Of course, it's good.

2362
01:29:27,428 --> 01:29:29,530
-Talk like a chef.
-We're asking you, Sam.

2363
01:29:29,597 --> 01:29:30,898
I think

2364
01:29:30,965 --> 01:29:31,999
this is a clever dish.

2365
01:29:32,066 --> 01:29:34,268
-Clever?
-It tastes Italian

2366
01:29:34,335 --> 01:29:36,637
and it's both sweet and salty.

2367
01:29:36,704 --> 01:29:39,207
They really brought out
the eggplant's texture.

2368
01:29:39,841 --> 01:29:41,609
-Even kids would love it.
-Right?

2369
01:29:41,676 --> 01:29:43,344
Kids would eat this.

2370
01:29:43,411 --> 01:29:46,347
Are you eating it too, Nam-no?
What's that in your hands?

2371
01:29:46,414 --> 01:29:47,615
Eggplant.

2372
01:29:47,682 --> 01:29:48,583
HOW ADORABLE

2373
01:29:48,649 --> 01:29:50,485
-It's mine. Yes.
-From the other team?

2374
01:29:50,551 --> 01:29:53,921
All right. The Chinese sisters' dish.

2375
01:29:53,988 --> 01:29:54,822
It's good.

2376
01:29:55,123 --> 01:29:56,090
YUM

2377
01:29:56,157 --> 01:29:57,692
CRUNCH

2378
01:29:57,759 --> 01:29:58,993
Don't just eat the peel.

2379
01:29:59,060 --> 01:30:00,428
It tastes Chinese.

2380
01:30:00,495 --> 01:30:02,130
Why didn't it turn soggy?

2381
01:30:02,196 --> 01:30:03,498
What's going on?

2382
01:30:04,165 --> 01:30:05,933
It's crispy on the outside,
soft on the inside.

2383
01:30:06,000 --> 01:30:07,001
It's so good.

2384
01:30:07,068 --> 01:30:08,369
What's this hint of spiciness?

2385
01:30:08,936 --> 01:30:09,904
It's spicy?

2386
01:30:09,971 --> 01:30:11,038
A dash of chili oil.

2387
01:30:11,105 --> 01:30:13,107
<i>She used chili oil?</i>

2388
01:30:13,174 --> 01:30:14,175
INTO THE BASI SAUCE

2389
01:30:14,242 --> 01:30:16,844
I just had the nest,
and it reminded me of a snack.

2390
01:30:16,911 --> 01:30:18,679
The long snack with seaweed on it.

2391
01:30:18,746 --> 01:30:21,416
-The thin one, right? It tastes like that.
-Right.

2392
01:30:21,482 --> 01:30:24,485
-It's good.
-Eggplants make great <i>basi</i>.

2393
01:30:25,453 --> 01:30:27,755
It still didn't taste like dessert.

2394
01:30:27,822 --> 01:30:30,024
It was like an actual dish.

2395
01:30:30,091 --> 01:30:32,493
The sweetness was subtle,

2396
01:30:32,560 --> 01:30:34,896
and it came with a crunch
when I bit on it,

2397
01:30:34,962 --> 01:30:36,464
<i>along with a bit of eggplant juice.</i>

2398
01:30:36,531 --> 01:30:39,100
Eggplant's flavor bursts in my mouth.

2399
01:30:39,167 --> 01:30:40,535
I can keep eating this.

2400
01:30:40,601 --> 01:30:42,703
As for the gelato,

2401
01:30:43,271 --> 01:30:45,373
it reminds me
of pudding from Southeast Asia.

2402
01:30:45,440 --> 01:30:48,209
-Rice pudding?
-Rice pudding.

2403
01:30:48,276 --> 01:30:50,878
-Like mango sticky rice.
-It's good.

2404
01:30:50,945 --> 01:30:52,547
It must be tough to choose.

2405
01:30:52,613 --> 01:30:54,682
-It is.
-Right?

2406
01:30:54,749 --> 01:30:58,085
Which side will she end up choosing?

2407
01:30:58,152 --> 01:31:00,154
<i>Press one for Moon-jung and Eun-yeong,</i>

2408
01:31:00,221 --> 01:31:02,423
<i>and two for Hyun-suk and Nam-no.</i>

2409
01:31:02,490 --> 01:31:05,393
Make your decision and press the button!

2410
01:31:06,327 --> 01:31:07,895
One, Chinese. Two, Western.

2411
01:31:08,796 --> 01:31:10,264
-Did you press it?
-Yes.

2412
01:31:10,331 --> 01:31:12,800
She had to make a tough choice.

2413
01:31:12,867 --> 01:31:15,770
So let's find out the result. Show us!

2414
01:31:15,837 --> 01:31:18,473
Ye-jin loves eggplant dishes,

2415
01:31:18,539 --> 01:31:21,742
and she wanted something new.
"Summer Eggplant Scent."

2416
01:31:21,809 --> 01:31:24,679
Will the Chinese sisters
get their revenge?

2417
01:31:24,745 --> 01:31:29,217
Or will Nam-no mooch off Hyun-suk
and take a star?

2418
01:31:29,283 --> 01:31:31,686
Who won?

2419
01:31:32,220 --> 01:31:33,888
Who did Ye-jin choose?

2420
01:31:35,256 --> 01:31:36,257
Ye-jin!

2421
01:31:36,324 --> 01:31:37,425
HYUN-SUK AND NAM-NO WINS

2422
01:31:37,625 --> 01:31:38,793
I TO YOU AM LIKE EGGPLANTS AT SUNSET WINS

2423
01:31:38,860 --> 01:31:40,795
Team Hyun-suk and Nam-no.

2424
01:31:40,862 --> 01:31:42,230
Hyun-suk and Nam-no.

2425
01:31:42,463 --> 01:31:43,598
HE MAKES A MOVE

2426
01:31:43,664 --> 01:31:44,999
AND HE COPIES

2427
01:31:45,066 --> 01:31:47,835
Hyun-suk drove the wagon

2428
01:31:47,902 --> 01:31:50,004
-and helped Nam-no win a star.
-Thank you.

2429
01:31:50,071 --> 01:31:51,973
THANK YOU

2430
01:31:52,039 --> 01:31:54,308
-That was a good ride.
-It was.

2431
01:31:54,375 --> 01:31:56,777
Chef Hyun-suk

2432
01:31:56,844 --> 01:32:00,248
has never lost a team round.

2433
01:32:00,314 --> 01:32:02,850
-He has won every single one.
-He's the best.

2434
01:32:02,917 --> 01:32:05,253
Whoever teams up with him wins a star.

2435
01:32:05,319 --> 01:32:07,488
-That's Hyun-suk.
-He's a star fairy.

2436
01:32:07,555 --> 01:32:09,924
-He's the best wagon driver.
-He is.

2437
01:32:10,825 --> 01:32:14,295
I was shocked that they made

2438
01:32:14,362 --> 01:32:17,365
such a high-quality dish
in that short time.

2439
01:32:17,431 --> 01:32:20,001
-The first bite I had of burrata…
-The lasagna.

2440
01:32:20,067 --> 01:32:24,071
<i>…and how it mixed with fig jam</i>

2441
01:32:24,138 --> 01:32:28,175
was somewhat familiar yet different,
which I appreciated.

2442
01:32:28,242 --> 01:32:30,978
The steak was perfect too.

2443
01:32:31,646 --> 01:32:32,947
So the <i>basi</i> was just…

2444
01:32:33,014 --> 01:32:35,082
It's something that I've always loved.

2445
01:32:35,149 --> 01:32:37,785
I know I can eat it endlessly,

2446
01:32:37,852 --> 01:32:40,288
but it was something

2447
01:32:40,354 --> 01:32:42,890
-more familiar.
-I see.

2448
01:32:42,957 --> 01:32:45,226
-But it was delicious.
-I see.

2449
01:32:45,293 --> 01:32:47,528
It must've been a difficult decision.

2450
01:32:47,595 --> 01:32:50,865
-Oh, the Chinese sisters.
-What a shame.

2451
01:32:50,932 --> 01:32:53,100
Next time we cook together,

2452
01:32:53,167 --> 01:32:56,637
we'll aim to be funny
instead of trying to win.

2453
01:32:56,704 --> 01:32:59,974
-Just dance next time.
-It's better to be funny.

2454
01:33:00,041 --> 01:33:00,942
That's true.

2455
01:33:01,008 --> 01:33:03,077
You two will each get the gift.

2456
01:33:03,144 --> 01:33:05,212
Yes! This one's for you, Mom.

2457
01:33:05,279 --> 01:33:07,381
-For the two of them.
-Great work.

2458
01:33:07,448 --> 01:33:10,351
-Should've given one and made them fight.
-Please put the stars on them.

2459
01:33:10,418 --> 01:33:12,853
-Hyun-suk had never lost a team round.
-Nam-no, you first.

2460
01:33:12,920 --> 01:33:15,356
Nam-no gets his fourth star!

2461
01:33:15,423 --> 01:33:16,891
Congratulations.

2462
01:33:16,958 --> 01:33:19,327
Hyun-suk is now
in double digits with ten stars!

2463
01:33:19,894 --> 01:33:21,062
SMUG

2464
01:33:22,597 --> 01:33:25,066
-Thank you.
-And please give them the present.

2465
01:33:25,132 --> 01:33:26,267
Congratulations!

2466
01:33:26,334 --> 01:33:28,102
COMING UP: THE PREVIEW

2467
01:33:28,169 --> 01:33:29,236
Good luck with your skincare.

2468
01:33:29,303 --> 01:33:32,206
Congratulations, you two.
You've won the team round.

2469
01:33:32,840 --> 01:33:33,808
I've lived far too long.

2470
01:33:33,874 --> 01:33:34,842
What is this nonsense?

2471
01:33:34,909 --> 01:33:35,943
It's a massive step down.

2472
01:33:36,010 --> 01:33:37,445
(IN TERMS OF GUESTS)

2473
01:33:37,979 --> 01:33:39,880
THE SPECIAL GUESTS
WHO LEFT EVERYONE SPEECHLESS

2474
01:33:40,047 --> 01:33:42,316
CHUSEOK SPECIAL:
KWON SUNG-JUN & YOON NAM-NO

2475
01:33:42,383 --> 01:33:43,484
Those Grubby Twins.

2476
01:33:43,551 --> 01:33:44,919
"Grubby Twins"?

2477
01:33:45,186 --> 01:33:46,053
EVERYONE PROTESTS

2478
01:33:46,120 --> 01:33:48,422
We'll break the highest rating.
I predict about 3.8%.

2479
01:33:48,489 --> 01:33:50,558
That's not an easy number to reach.

2480
01:33:50,625 --> 01:33:52,026
I'll shave my head if we do.

2481
01:33:52,093 --> 01:33:53,227
Hey!

2482
01:33:53,294 --> 01:33:54,462
We're one.

2483
01:33:54,528 --> 01:33:56,030
EVEN PLEDGING TO SHAVE HIS HEAD

2484
01:33:56,597 --> 01:33:59,200
PRESENTING THE CHEFS' FRIDGES

2485
01:33:59,266 --> 01:34:01,035
-Carabineros and scampi.
-Scampi?

2486
01:34:01,102 --> 01:34:02,870
SWEETBREAD (LAMB THYMUS),
OSSOBUCO (VEAL SHANK)

2487
01:34:02,937 --> 01:34:05,373
-This is way too staged.
-What is it?

2488
01:34:05,439 --> 01:34:06,407
I can't do this.

2489
01:34:07,842 --> 01:34:09,310
FIRST EVER FRIDGE BOYCOTT?

2490
01:34:09,377 --> 01:34:10,511
SUNG-JUN, THIS IS THE REAL DEAL!

2491
01:34:11,145 --> 01:34:12,546
NAM-NO'S AUTHENTIC, REAL FRIDGE

2492
01:34:12,613 --> 01:34:14,015
What's this good with?

2493
01:34:14,081 --> 01:34:15,383
That anchovy <i>kal-guksu ramyeon…</i>

2494
01:34:16,350 --> 01:34:17,918
NAM-NO'S WINNING ICE CREAM PAIRING

2495
01:34:17,985 --> 01:34:19,153
This is great.

2496
01:34:19,353 --> 01:34:21,322
THE BEST FOODIE OF THE SHOW

2497
01:34:21,389 --> 01:34:22,823
Can Nam-no just cook for us?

2498
01:34:23,024 --> 01:34:24,692
NOPE, I'M HERE TO EAT TODAY!

2499
01:34:24,759 --> 01:34:25,626
TODAY, THE CHEFS ARE THE GUESTS

2500
01:34:25,826 --> 01:34:27,528
A COOK-OFF FOR THE CHEFS

2501
01:34:27,695 --> 01:34:29,096
A DISH ONLY FOR SUNG-JUN

2502
01:34:29,330 --> 01:34:31,065
AND A DISH THAT DEPICTS SUNG-JUN

2503
01:34:31,532 --> 01:34:32,700
WHY ME?

2504
01:34:32,933 --> 01:34:33,968
THE MASTER'S HEARTFELT TOUCH

2505
01:34:34,168 --> 01:34:36,604
MATCHING THE DOUGH WITH HIS FACE

2506
01:34:36,671 --> 01:34:38,372
He's depicting him as much as possible.

2507
01:34:38,673 --> 01:34:39,640
A COOK-OFF JUST FOR NAM-NO,

2508
01:34:39,840 --> 01:34:41,208
A 2:2 TEAM MATCH

2509
01:34:41,409 --> 01:34:42,810
A HUGE SERVING, PERFECT FOR THE GUEST

2510
01:34:42,877 --> 01:34:44,311
You're making a dumpling that big?

2511
01:34:44,378 --> 01:34:46,080
THE GUEST LOOKS ECSTATIC

2512
01:34:46,247 --> 01:34:47,081
YUM!

2513
01:34:47,882 --> 01:34:48,849
DELISH!

2514
01:34:49,283 --> 01:34:50,551
DECIDES TO BINGE

2515
01:34:50,618 --> 01:34:52,119
He can fit that in his mouth?

2516
01:34:52,186 --> 01:34:53,120
TOTALLY

2517
01:34:53,354 --> 01:34:54,255
IN AWE

2518
01:34:54,455 --> 01:34:57,458
LIKE A FAMILY WATCHING A NEPHEW
DEVOUR THE FOOD DURING THE HOLIDAYS

2519
01:34:57,625 --> 01:35:00,161
WHICH DISH DOES NAM-NO THE FOODIE
LIKE THE MOST?

2520
01:35:04,365 --> 01:35:05,633
It's different when she does it.

2521
01:35:05,700 --> 01:35:07,501
-Like feeding cold medicine.
-She just stuffed him.

2522
01:35:07,568 --> 01:35:09,537
-This is delicious, Mom.
-Look at him.

2523
01:35:19,547 --> 01:35:24,318
Subtitle translation by: Eunsook Youn
